# fapolicyd trust notes for maknae -> /etc/fapolicyd/trust.d/maknae
#
# The rpm-installed /usr/bin/maknaed is trusted AUTOMATICALLY by fapolicyd's
# rpmdb trust backend (every file owned by an installed rpm is trusted) — no
# per-file record is needed, and none is shipped here on purpose: a static
# `path size sha256` record would go stale on every rebuild, and a bare path is
# not a valid trust record (fapolicyd would silently ignore it).
#
# Verified: on a STIG-hardened enforcing host the rpm-installed daemon executes
# under fapolicyd via rpmdb trust (Tokki PR-T1 acceptance, Rocky 10).
#
# FUTURE tool-exec path (out-of-rpmdb binaries, e.g. an operator-dropped helper):
# register each explicitly with a properly-hashed record —
#     sudo fapolicyd-cli --file add /path/to/binary
#     sudo fapolicyd-cli --update
# Do NOT hand-edit a bare path into this file expecting it to take effect.
